---
// /prototypes/air-exchange-rate-responsive — the COMBINED presentation of Option B.
// Not a fork and not a third design: it is the same smaqmd-aer-wizard component in
// its `responsive` variant, so the steps, the fields and the whole calc engine are
// literally the same code as the wizard and mobile views and cannot drift from them.
//
// It merges the two existing views along the one axis that actually depends on
// screen width — the isometric scene, which needs room to read. Wide screens get
// the wizard composition (scene behind, flow floating over it); below 68rem the
// scene is hidden and its animation loop paused on every step but the result,
// where it returns as a band above the card, leaving the mobile flow. The
// opening fork slide is shown at EVERY width, so both audiences (checking a
// cleaner vs shopping for one) meet the same single question first, and the
// controls stay `lg` throughout — one page cannot know whether the pointer is a
// thumb, so it takes the touch-safe size everywhere.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SmaqmdAerWizard from '../../components/smaqmd-aer-wizard.astro';
import SmaqmdLogoLink from '../../components/smaqmd-logo-link.astro';
---
<!-- manifest:
  layout: component-owned (fixed overlay when wide, single flowed column when narrow)
  sections:
    - district logo      -> smaqmd-logo-link (href) to airquality.org
    - page h1            -> smaqmd-aer-wizard slot="header" (visible h1; the wizard's own headings start at h2)
    - opening slide      -> smaqmd-aer-wizard (replaces esa-page-header)
    - wizard steps       -> smaqmd-aer-wizard variant="responsive" (scene wide-only, lg controls)
-->
<BaseLayout title="Air Exchange Rate Tool (Responsive) — SMAQMD">
  <main>
    <SmaqmdAerWizard variant="responsive">
      <!-- THE HEADER SLOT — the logo home link over the page h1.

           THE PAGE h1. The wizard's headings all start at h2 (it is a section, and
           the same component also ships inside the standalone build, where a host
           page supplies the h1), and this page drops esa-page-header because the
           opening slide carries the visible title — so without this the document
           would have no top-level heading at all. VISIBLE, and slotted here rather
           than loose in <main>: the wide layout is a fixed-overlay composition, so
           a flowed h1 outside the wizard would add a scroll strip beside it. The
           header slot already rides the `placeHeader` relocation in the wizard
           script, so when the layout goes narrow the title lands above the scene.

           No esa-page-header: its title and lede would restate the opening slide,
           which this variant shows at every width. The slide owns the question;
           the h1 owns the document heading.

           No version toggle either. The switcher's other destinations all carry a
           page header and no intro slide, so toggling INTO this page would
           silently drop the chrome the toggle itself lives in.

           The logo links to airquality.org (the agency-mark convention;
           requested 2026-09-02), which means this page has NO link back to the
           prototype library — it replaced the "Prototype library" back button.
           Deliberate: the production deliverable is embedded in a host page
           where the library doesn't exist, so the prototype mirrors that.

           A .cluster, deliberately NOT a .stack: a stack stretches its children,
           which would blow the logo's <a> out to the full column width and make
           the empty space beside the logo a link target. The cluster lays logo
           and h1 on a row, centers them, and wraps at narrow widths. -->
      <div slot="header" class="cluster" data-gap="md">
        <SmaqmdLogoLink />
        <h1 class="typography-heading-lg smaqmd-aerb__page-title">Air Exchange Rate Tool</h1>
      </div>
    </SmaqmdAerWizard>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
